## Step 5: 🚨 Critical Alerts Page

Here's the complete Streamlit code snippet for your Critical Alerts analytics page:

```python
import streamlit as st

# Placeholder Data (replace with real-time alert system)
critical_alerts = [
    {"type": "warning", "message": "API Latency High", "timestamp": "2025-05-12 10:45"},
    {"type": "success", "message": "System Operational", "timestamp": "2025-05-12 10:30"},
    {"type": "warning", "message": "High Liability on Bot B", "timestamp": "2025-05-12 10:15"}
]

# Page Title
st.title("🚨 Critical Alerts")

# Display Alerts
for alert in critical_alerts:
    if alert["type"] == "warning":
        st.warning(f"{alert['timestamp']} - {alert['message']}")
    elif alert["type"] == "success":
        st.success(f"{alert['timestamp']} - {alert['message']}")

# Alert Count Summary
st.subheader("Alert Summary")
alert_summary = {"Warnings": sum(1 for alert in critical_alerts if alert["type"] == "warning"),
                 "Successes": sum(1 for alert in critical_alerts if alert["type"] == "success")}
st.bar_chart(alert_summary)
```

